      "writtenOn": "2025-06-06T19:16:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking more at this... We don\u0027t really support setting the root table more than once (since we only call activate_iommu() once), yet we allow the host to change root_pa, and even to undonate the root table?\n\nI don\u0027t think we need to support changing the root table, so it would be much simpler if we just explicitly disallowed calling PKVM_HC_IOMMU_SET_RTA more than once? (Maybe even renamed it to PKVM_HC_IOMMU_ACTIVATE? and/or let it enable translation right away, as I suggested in another comment?)",
      "revId": "91bfca5b49146677f20cb22bbf52310d073e42cc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
